## [Relics](relics)

### [The Cipher](cipher)
---
Atmosphere: purple
Containment: tractor
Scrape band: 160
Margin: 90
Forbid jump: yes
Seed: 68
Art: plain_asteroid_6, plain_asteroid_8, plain_asteroid_11
---
A relay the giants sank in a nebula, and then hid inside. Nothing here is square and
nothing here is straight.

### [the false mouth](false_mouth)
---
Relic: cipher
Chamber: -2400, 0, 0, 700
---
The obvious way in, and it goes nowhere - a bubble with one exit, and the exit is the way
you came. Whoever hid this expected somebody to find the hole and stop looking.

### [the throat](throat)
---
Relic: cipher
Chamber: -1200, -600, 800, 600
Passage to: false_mouth 300
---
The real route, off the floor of the false mouth and behind it.

### [the coil](coil)
---
Relic: cipher
Chamber: 400, -900, 1600, 1000
Passage to: throat 320
---
The relay's own body. Everything else in here is a corridor to this.

### [the sump](sump)
---
Relic: cipher
Chamber: 900, -2300, 900, 800
Passage to: coil 280
---
Below the coil, and full of whatever settled out of the nebula over a thousand years.

### [the spill](spill)
---
Relic: cipher
Chamber: -150, -1450, 850, 500
Passage to: throat 260, sump 260
---
The long way down. It drops out of the throat before the coil and comes up under the
sump, which makes this the only structure in the Beacon with a way ROUND its middle - and
that is the whole of the puzzle here. Everything else the Torgoth built is a chain.

### [the keying chamber](keying)
---
Relic: cipher
Chamber: 1900, -700, 2600, 900
Passage to: coil 300
---
Where the Cipher sits. The only room in the structure with a hard floor.

### [the collapsed throat](throat_fall)
---
Relic: cipher
Barrier: -400, -750, 1200, 420
Clear with: beam
---
A fall of the relay's own shielding, jammed across the short way into the coil. It can be
cut - it is only a few meters of plate and a suit carries a torch - and while somebody is
cutting it the rest of the party is standing still.

Or take the spill, down past the sump and up the other side.

**A shut way with no way round is a wait; a shut way with a way round is a decision.**
Measured on the web this file builds: cutting through is 6404 units to the housing, and
the spill is 6824 - about nine seconds at cruise, against the twelve a cut costs. The two
are deliberately close, so neither is the obvious answer.

What separates them is what you SEE. The spill passes within 911 units of the sump floor,
close enough to light the salvage lying on it; a party that cut their way in stays 1700
away and never learns the room had anything in it. The reward for the slow way is not a
shortcut later - it is the thing you would not have found.

